what is aws egress-only internet gateways 

egress-only internet gateways is used for ipv6 internet access in your private subnet 
this mean you have private subnet where you hosted your aws instances that you want it to access
internet. if your instances are ipv4 you can use Nat gateways but if you use ipv6 you can use 
egress-only internet gateways which is stateful mean it will allow returned request and you 
can only ask the request mean it allows outbound internet traffic only not inbound traffic


